// Mutating a node after the fact. The parser needs this in two places: a
// `goto` is resolved to a block number only once the whole function has
// been read, and a forward-declared struct's size is filled in when its
// definition arrives.
//
// An imported list cannot be index-assigned directly -- `(import na)[i] = v`
// parses as a comparison and silently does nothing. Passing the list as a
// parameter makes the target a plain identifier again, and lists have
// reference semantics, so the store is shared with every other holder.
//
// get/ has no room for a sibling file, so this file was promoted into its
// own subdirectory to make room for the zero-argument readers (read1.id,
// stl0.id) a case here or in mk/push/ needs to observe what changed.

m_of(int id) {
  int[] m = (import nm)[id];
} return int[] m;
given lm_fixture (0):([3])
given boot_a given exprfix stdin "1;" ((import extop)):([])

set_a(int id, int a) {
  lset((import na), id, a);
} return void;
given boot_a given exprfix stdin "1;" (0, 99):() then a0_of:(99)
given boot_a given exprfix stdin "2;" (0, 55):() then a0_of:(55)

